# Kademi server JS: Nashorn (.js)

This file runs **inside the Kademi platform**, in a sandboxed Nashorn engine. It is not Node.
This is the legacy engine: maintain existing apps here, but write new apps on GraalJS
(`engineVersion="2.0"` and `.mjs`). Switching an existing app is a rewrite of every file, not a
config change - do not start one incidentally.

- **Target ES5.1 and declare variables with `var`.** `let` and `const` work only when
  `controllers.xml` sets `engineVersion="1.1"` explicitly. Avoid arrow functions, `class`,
  template literals, destructuring and `for...of`.
- **`formatter.foreach(...)` instead of a native loop.** Native loops do not yield, so the CPU
  governor cannot interrupt a runaway request.
- **Never `===` against a Java value.** A Kademi id arrives as a Java `Long`, so `===` against a
  JS number is always false. Use `formatter.eq(a, b)`, and `formatter.isNull` / `isEmpty` /
  `isEqual` / `gt` / `lt` for the rest.
- **`formatter.toJson(obj)`, not `JSON.stringify`, for any Java object** - it returns `{}`.
- **`log.info('saved {} for {}', id, userId)` with `{}` placeholders.** Not `console.log`, not
  `print`.
- **No `Java.type`, no `java.*`, no fully-qualified class names** - class filtering blocks them at
  runtime. Use `formatter.newMap()`, `formatter.newArrayList()` or a `services.*` method.
- **Nothing mutable at global scope.** App instances are shared across accounts.
- Functions referenced only by name from `.addMethod('GET', 'myFn')` look unused to a linter. They
  are not.

`services`, `formatter`, `controllerMappings`, `views` and `page` are Java objects dispatched
dynamically - nothing checks a method name until that line runs. Confirm any member at
`https://docs.kademi.co/ref/templating/md/<ClassName>.md` before calling it.

Full guidance: the `kademi-server-js` skill, and its `references/nashorn.md`.
